<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 12.28 bln levs of 1-, 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 12.28 bln levs of 1-, 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Monday sold two discount T-bill issues with maturities of one and four weeks, yielding 3.65 percent and 17.56 percent to maturity, respectively, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Bids were received for a total of 12.317 billion levs of T-bills, but the ministry approved bids for 12.277 billion levs worth.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3012497007	 BG3012597004</p>
<p> Term			    one week	     four weeks</p>
<p> Auction date		  January 27, 1997   January 27, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date		    January 27, 1997   January 27, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 February 3, 1997   February 24, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		 8,016.9 million levs   4,300 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.48 pct	    85.06 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 7,976.9 million levs   4,300 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.48 pct	    85.06 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity	3.65 pct	    17.56 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
